{
  "_comment": "Canonical cross-runtime hilo:v1 test vectors. Reproducible by any runtime (native Rust, wasm, TS) from the pinned algorithm below. All values are integer/ppm; no floating point. Generated by an independent python3 reference: libs/games/scripts/gen_vectors.py.",
  "algorithm": {
    "game_type": "hilo:v1",
    "derivation": "v1",
    "seed_derivation": "digest(decision, chunk) = blake2b-256 of b'99dot5:engine-seed:v1' (21 bytes, no terminator) || u8 len(game_type) || game_type || u8 len(server_seed) || server_seed || u8 len(client_seed) || client_seed || decision u32 LE || chunk u32 LE. The three text fields are their ASCII bytes as fed to the engine (the 64-hex strings in production) and may not exceed 255 bytes. A decision's randomness is read sequentially from chunk 0, 32 bytes per chunk, at most 4 chunks (128 bytes). preimage_example_hex is the preimage for game_type 'hilo:v1', server_seed '11'*32, client_seed '22'*32, decision 3, chunk 1. hilo:v1: the opening card is decision 0; the state carries decision_index, 1 after the bet and +1 per guess, and a guess draws its card under decision decision_index. A partial-cashout, cashout or abandon draws nothing and moves nothing, so a bank no longer shifts later cards",
    "preimage_example_hex": "",
    "preimage_example_digest_hex": "e032790ea31b22d5299594aa1de0d461e67cc3b398d5aec5d4685d98684599db",
    "card": "raw_u64 = little-endian u64 of the decision's stream bytes [0..8]; deck_index = (raw_u64 * 52) >> 64 (Lemire wide-reduction, no modulo bias); rank = deck_index % 13 (0=Ace .. 12=King, ace low), suit = deck_index / 13 (0=clubs, 1=diamonds, 2=hearts, 3=spades)",
    "rank_numeric": "rank index + 1 (Ace=1 .. King=13)",
    "probabilities": "higher_or_equal_count = 14 - rank_numeric; lower_or_equal_count = rank_numeric; probability_ppm = half_up(count * 1e6 / 13)",
    "multipliers": "fair_ppm = half_up(1e6 * 1e6 / probability_ppm); offered_ppm = half_up(fair_ppm * 995000 / 1e6). Both directions computed each step from the CURRENT card; the guess pays the multiplier quoted on the card it was made against",
    "win_rule": "higher wins iff next_rank >= current_rank; lower wins iff next_rank <= current_rank (an equal rank wins BOTH directions)",
    "cumulative": "starts at 1e6 on place-bet; each winning guess multiplies: cum = half_up(cum * step_multiplier_ppm / 1e6); a losing guess sets 0 and settles the round",
    "payout": "the value model is a (banked, live) pair in integer micro-tez: live starts at stake * 1e6 and each winning guess folds live' = half_up(live * step_multiplier_ppm / 1e6). The system 'partial-cashout' action (borsh payload: amount u128 LE, in the asset's atomic units) moves amount from live to banked without touching the multiplier chain \u2014 note it consumes an action index, shifting every later card draw. Cashout and the system 'abandon' action pay banked + live (abandon settles abandoned but at the position's current value, sec-28); a lost guess pays banked (never less: the banked part is already the player's)",
    "house_edge_ppm": 995000,
    "scale_ppm": 1000000,
    "rounding": "half-up (midpoint away from zero), mirroring game-engine-core/src/fixed_point.rs",
    "hex_scenarios": "Seeds in the production form: server_seed_hex is 64 lowercase hex chars and the engine's client seed is effective_client_seed_hex = lowercase hex of blake2b-256(client_seed_text) (the client seed is hashed once, at bet time); both hex strings are fed to derive_seed as text. Each entry's server_seed_hex = hex(blake2b-256(b'<name>-<search_index>')), where search_index is the smallest N >= 0 for which the entry's predicate holds. Each hilo entry records the first two steps under the hex seeds, winning_direction_at_1 ('higher' or 'lower'; a tie wins both directions and is recorded as 'higher'), and raw_text_card_0: the opening card if the raw client_seed_text were (wrongly) used as the client seed"
  },
